/E (Sampling is simply stated as selecting a portion of the population in the research area, which will be a representation of the whole population. The usual goal in sampling is to produce a representative sample, that is, a sample that is similar to the population on all characteristics, except that it includes fewer people because it is a sample rather than the complete population. Simple random sampling was used in order to select the samples. A simple random sample is meant to be an unbiased representation of a group. It is the most basic sampling procedure to draw the sample.)
